      <!-- SECTION 6: FAQ -->
      <section class="section" id="faq" style="border-top: 2px solid var(--border); padding-top: 40px; margin-top: 40px;">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
        
        <p>
          Entering the acrylic emulsion and paint manufacturing business involves addressing complex questions across polymer chemistry, factory licensing, financial capital, and process engineering. Below are comprehensive, professionally validated answers to the most common questions encountered by chemical entrepreneurs, procurement officers, and plant managers.
        </p>

        <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 20px;">
          <div class="box" style="margin: 0; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: 20px;">
            <h3 style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.15rem; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px; border: none; padding-bottom: 0;">1. What is the minimum investment required to start a small-scale acrylic emulsion plant?</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
              Setting up a basic 2-5 ton/day emulsion plant typically requires an investment between ₹85 Lakhs to ₹2.1 Crores, depending on land costs and automation levels. A simple paint formulation unit (buying emulsion, mixing paint) can be started for as low as ₹12 Lakhs - ₹25 Lakhs.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="box" style="margin: 0; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: 20px;">
            <h3 style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.15rem; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px; border: none; padding-bottom: 0;">2. Can I manufacture both pure acrylics and styrene acrylics in the same reactor?</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
              Yes, the reactor hardware is versatile. However, you must have rigorous cleaning protocols (CIP) to prevent cross-contamination, especially when switching between styrene-based and pure acrylic batches.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="box" style="margin: 0; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: 20px;">
            <h3 style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.15rem; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px; border: none; padding-bottom: 0;">3. What are the main regulatory licenses needed in India?</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
              You will typically need a Pollution Control Board (PCB) "Consent to Operate," Factory License, GST registration, and compliance with local fire safety and waste disposal (ETP) regulations.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="box" style="margin: 0; background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius-md); padding: 20px;">
            <h3 style="color: var(--primary); font-size: 1.15rem; margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8px; border: none; padding-bottom: 0;">4. How do I reduce the VOC content of my emulsion?</h3>
            <p style="margin: 0; line-height: 1.6;">
              You can use advanced stripping techniques (vacuum stripping) at the end of the polymerization process to remove unreacted monomers, or use high-conversion redox initiators to ensure &gt;99.9% monomer conversion.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
